{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"To bring this to a close, I was in the evening—where?—at Mozart’s *The Marriage of Figaro*. The Kleins stayed on Sunday for that reason. I had to admit to myself that the Italian voices in this more restrained music did not seem to have as much opportunity to develop their brilliant runs, which had been so sweet to hear; but in themselves, with what perfection were the arias, duets, etc., especially the recitatives, delivered—the latter are entirely the artist’s own natural creations. Lablache, what a Figaro! Fodor as Susanna—she would indeed have had to be more beautiful and taller for this role. Signora Dardanelli as the Countess; I sat closer to the stage this time than the first time I saw her—what a beautiful woman, a lovely Italian head, and a calmness, nobility in posture and action—very lovely, beautiful decorum—I almost fell into your situation and would have fallen in love with this woman! She is in fact most charming. Donzelli as the Count—compared rather unfavorably to her; such situations are not good for him."}}],"created":1795080338,"model":"qwen","system_fingerprint":"b11429-d81235049","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":239,"prompt_tokens":341,"total_tokens":580,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-ERFlmdVilgSysGX0fgZQPFjFbZ70VGcl","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":341,"prompt_ms":550.878,"prompt_per_token_ms":1.6154780058651028,"prompt_per_second":619.0118320208829,"predicted_n":239,"predicted_ms":5710.868,"predicted_per_token_ms":23.995243697478994,"predicted_per_second":41.674925773104896}}